{{ if project["backend.llm"] == "azure-openai" ~}}
- Embeddings use the same Azure OpenAI resource and key, and the deployment named by the AppHost's parameter `azure-openai-embedding-deployment` (`text-embedding-3-small` by default), which must exist in that resource. Against OpenAI's `https://api.openai.com/v1`, it names an OpenAI embedding model instead.{{ else ~}}
- Point the AppHost at your Azure OpenAI resource for embeddings and give it the resource's key, which stays out of the repository: `dotnet user-secrets set Parameters:azure-openai-endpoint https://<resource>.openai.azure.com --project src/AppHost` and `dotnet user-secrets set Parameters:azure-openai-api-key <key> --project src/AppHost`. The parameter `azure-openai-embedding-deployment` (`text-embedding-3-small` by default) must name a deployment in that resource. Without them the host cannot embed text; the tests never need them. To run locally against OpenAI instead, with an OpenAI key, set `azure-openai-endpoint` to `https://api.openai.com/v1`, `azure-openai-api-key` to the OpenAI key and `azure-openai-embedding-deployment` to a model name: an endpoint that already ends in `/v1` is used as is.{{ end }}